From 1b72da8510a3beb33106f776441dff486bf24269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:07:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 182/206] F152: move Isolate::simulator_ to +0x20, use R5 in
 safepoint stubs

Shorebird's Isolate places simulator_ right after finalizers_ (+0x20);
ours had it after environment_callback_ (+0xa0). Moving it makes the
four stubs that load Isolate::simulator_offset() (CallSimulatorFromFfi-
Trampoline, ResumeOnSimulator, RunDartOnCPU, TransitionDartToSimulator-
IfNeeded) byte-identical to theirs, and aligns the 14 pointer members
from scheduled_mutator_thread_ to environment_callback_ with their
offsets (DWARF-verified in ProductSimIosARM64).

EnterSafepoint/ExitSafepoint load+call the runtime entry through R5
instead of R0, matching Shorebird's stubs. Both stub bodies are wrapped
in PushRegisters/PopRegisters(all general registers) and R5 is not read
between the push and the ldr, so this is encoding-only.

The move shifts has_resumption_breakpoints_ (+0x20 -> +0x28 on 64-bit,
+0x10 -> +0x14 on 32-bit). That field is in runtime_offsets_list.h under
NOT_IN_PRODUCT, so all 15 non-PRODUCT entries in
runtime_offsets_extracted.h are updated; without this CheckOffsets
aborts non-PRODUCT builds (observed in a DebugSIMARM64 build).
Only the macos simarm64 JIT table was verified by CheckOffsets; the
other 14 entries follow from the same ABI layout arithmetic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

